,"page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#2-collect-signups","content":"`consent.ip`, `consent.userAgent`, `consent.text` you pass, stored on the contact with source `api`"},"7705":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-57","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#2-collect-signups","content":"Topics"},"7706":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-58","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#2-collect-signups","content":"The form's list (and its topic)"},"7707":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-59","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#2-collect-signups","content":"Any `listIds` and `topicIds`"},"7708":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-60","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#2-collect-signups","content":"Never put your API key in browser code. If the signup happens in the browser and you want the API's features, post to your own backend and call the API from there."},"7709":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-61","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#subscribing-from-your-backend","content":"In Python (`northrelay` 1.9.0 is async):"},"7710":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-62","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#subscribing-from-your-backend","content":"Or with `curl`:"},"7711":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-63","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#subscribing-from-your-backend","content":"The call is idempotent: calling it again for someone already on the list returns `200` and adds nothing."},"7712":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-64","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#subscribing-from-your-backend","content":"Handle these errors in your signup handler:"},"7713":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-65","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#subscribing-from-your-backend","content":"Code"},"7714":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-66","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#subscribing-from-your-backend","content":"What to tell the user"},"7715":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-67","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#subscribing-from-your-backend","content":"`RECIPIENT_UNSUBSCRIBED`"},"7716":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-68","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#subscribing-from-your-backend","content":"They unsubscribed earlier. If they are signing up again now, that is fresh consent: retry with `\"resubscribe\": true` and `\"doubleOptIn\": true`."},"7717":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-69","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#subscribing-from-your-backend","content":"`RECIPIENT_SUPPRESSED`"},"7718":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-70","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#subscribing-from-your-backend","content":"The address bounced or reported spam. Ask for a different address."},"7719":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-71","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#subscribing-from-your-backend","content":"`CONTACT_BLOCKED`"},"7720":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-72","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#subscribing-from-your-backend","content":"Same as above; this address cannot be re-added through the API."},"7721":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-73","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#subscribing-from-your-backend","content":"`FREE_TIER_CONTACT_LIMIT`"},"7722":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-74","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#subscribing-from-your-backend","content":"Your account is at its contact limit; upgrade the plan."},"7723":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-75","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#3-double-opt-in","content":"With `doubleOptIn: true`:"},"7724":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-76","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#3-double-opt-in","content":"The contact is created as `PENDING` and added to the lists. Campaigns skip it while it is `PENDING`."},"7725":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-77","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#3-double-opt-in","content":"NorthRelay emails a confirmation link (`https://app.northrelay.ca/c/<token>`, valid for 7 days). Pass `confirmationTemplateId` to use your own template; it can use `{{confirm_url}}`, `{{first_name}}`, `{{last_name}}` and `{{email}}`."},"7726":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-78","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#3-double-opt-in","content":"The recipient clicks; the contact becomes `ACTIVE`, the `contact.confirmed` webhook fires, and the browser is redirected to your `redirectUrl` (`https://` only)."},"7727":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-79","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#3-double-opt-in","content":"If someone says the email never arrived, call `POST /api/v1/subscriptions/{email}/resend-confirmation`. It re-sends the email and gives the link another 7 days."},"7728":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-80","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#3-double-opt-in","content":"Double opt-in is the strongest consent record you can have, and it keeps typos and bots off your list, which protects your deliverability. Use it for anything public-facing."},"7729":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-81","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#4-keep-consent-evidence-casl-and-gdpr","content":"Canada's anti-spam law (CASL) and the EU's GDPR expect you to show when and how each person agreed to receive marketing mail. For every API subscribe call and every signup form submission, NorthRelay stores on the contact:"},"7730":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-82","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#4-keep-consent-evidence-casl-and-gdpr","content":"Field"},"7731":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-83","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#4-keep-consent-evidence-casl-and-gdpr","content":"Source"},"7732":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-84","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#4-keep-consent-evidence-casl-and-gdpr","content":"`consentSource`"},"7733":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-85","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#4-keep-consent-evidence-casl-and-gdpr","content":"How they subscribed: `api`, `form`, `import`, `preference_center`"},"7734":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-86","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#4-keep-consent-evidence-casl-and-gdpr","content":"`consentAt`"},"7735":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-87","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#4-keep-consent-evidence-casl-and-gdpr","content":"When"},"7736":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-88","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#4-keep-consent-evidence-casl-and-gdpr","content":"`consentIp`, `consentUserAgent`"},"7737":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-89","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#4-keep-consent-evidence-casl-and-gdpr","content":"What you passed in `consent` (signup forms record the submitting browser)"},"7738":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-90","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#4-keep-consent-evidence-casl-and-gdpr","content":"`consentText`"},"7739":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-91","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#4-keep-consent-evidence-casl-and-gdpr","content":"The wording they agreed to (signup forms record `Signup form: <form name>`)"},"7740":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-92","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#4-keep-consent-evidence-casl-and-gdpr","content":"`confirmedAt`"},"7741":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-93","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#4-keep-consent-evidence-casl-and-gdpr","content":"When they confirmed the double opt-in"},"7742":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-94","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#4-keep-consent-evidence-casl-and-gdpr","content":"Pass `consent.text` with the exact label of the checkbox or button the person used, and pass their IP from your server (NorthRelay only sees your server's address). Read it back at any time:"},"7743":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-95","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#4-keep-consent-evidence-casl-and-gdpr","content":"This guide is not legal advice; check what your jurisdiction and audience require."},"7744":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-96","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#5-a-preference-page-inside-your-product","content":"Let signed-in users manage their email from your own settings screen. Read the current state with `GET /subscriptions/{email}` and save their choices with `PATCH /subscriptions/{email}`."},"7745":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-97","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#5-a-preference-page-inside-your-product","content":"Render a checkbox per topic (use `label` and `description`, falling back to `name`), and a \"Unsubscribe from all marketing email\" option. On save, send only what changed:"},"7746":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-98","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#5-a-preference-page-inside-your-product","content":"Things to know:"},"7747":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-99","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#5-a-preference-page-inside-your-product","content":"`GET` returns `200` with `contact: null` for someone who never subscribed, so the page works for every user."},"7748":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-100","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#5-a-preference-page-inside-your-product","content":"`topics` lists every topic in your account. If some are internal, filter them out."},"7749":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-101","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#5-a-preference-page-inside-your-product","content":"Turning a topic back on does not undo \"unsubscribe from all\". To bring someone back, the user has to opt in again; then call `POST /subscriptions` (or `PATCH` with `lists`) with `\"resubscribe\": true` and fresh `consent`."},"7750":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-102","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#6-unsubscribe-links-and-one-click-unsubscribe","content":"Every marketing message needs a working unsubscribe link, and Gmail, Yahoo and Outlook require RFC 8058 one-click unsubscribe headers for bulk senders. NorthRelay handles both:"},"7751":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-103","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#6-unsubscribe-links-and-one-click-unsubscribe","content":"**Campaigns:** put `{{unsubscribe_url}}` in your template footer. NorthRelay adds the `List-Unsubscribe` and `List-Unsubscribe-Post: List-Unsubscribe=One-Click` headers to every message."},"7752":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-104","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#6-unsubscribe-links-and-one-click-unsubscribe","content":"**Preference link:** put `{{preferences_url}}` next to it to give recipients a signed link to NorthRelay's hosted preference centre, where they can choose topics or unsubscribe from everything."},"7753":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-105","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#6-unsubscribe-links-and-one-click-unsubscribe","content":"**API mail on a marketing message stream:** NorthRelay injects the unsubscribe footer and the same headers automatically. Unsubscribes from these messages are attributed to your account and fire `contact.unsubscribed`, even when the recipient is not one of your contacts."},"7754":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-106","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#6-unsubscribe-links-and-one-click-unsubscribe","content":"When a mailbox provider's \"Unsubscribe\" button is pressed, NorthRelay unsubscribes the recipient from all marketing mail and fires `contact.unsubscribed` with `method: \"one_click\"`. A plain `GET` of the one-click URL never unsubscribes anyone, because security scanners prefetch links."},"7755":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-107","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#7-hosting-your-own-unsubscribe-page","content":"NorthRelay's hosted unsubscribe and preference pages work out of the box. If you would rather keep recipients on your own domain for campaign mail, link to your page and pass along the NorthRelay link:"},"7756":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-108","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#7-hosting-your-own-unsubscribe-page","content":"The unsubscribe link has the form `https://track.north-pipe.ca/u/{token}`. Your page takes the last path segment as the token, asks the recipient what they want, and posts it to the public endpoint (no API key; the token is the authentication):"},"7757":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-109","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#7-hosting-your-own-unsubscribe-page","content":"Notes:"},"7758":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-110","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#7-hosting-your-own-unsubscribe-page","content":"Tokens are signed and expire. `INVALID_TOKEN` means the link is too old or was altered."},"7759":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-111","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#7-hosting-your-own-unsubscribe-page","content":"The page must not unsubscribe on page load (link scanners open it). Do it when the recipient presses a button."},"7760":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-112","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#7-hosting-your-own-unsubscribe-page","content":"The `List-Unsubscribe` header still points at NorthRelay, so one-click from the mailbox provider keeps working without your page."},"7761":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-113","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#7-hosting-your-own-unsubscribe-page","content":"For opt-outs made by a signed-in user in your product, skip the token and call `POST /api/v1/subscriptions/unsubscribe` from your server with your API key."},"7762":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-114","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#8-keep-your-app-in-sync-with-webhooks","content":"Register one webhook endpoint for the contact and list events, and optionally engagement events:"},"7763":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-115","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#8-keep-your-app-in-sync-with-webhooks","content":"Event"},"7764":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-116","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#8-keep-your-app-in-sync-with-webhooks","content":"Typical use"},"7765":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-117","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#8-keep-your-app-in-sync-with-webhooks","content":"`contact.subscribed`"},"7766":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-118","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#8-keep-your-app-in-sync-with-webhooks","content":"Mark the user as \"newsletter: pending\" or \"subscribed\" (`details.status`)"},"7767":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-119","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#8-keep-your-app-in-sync-with-webhooks","content":"`contact.confirmed`"},"7768":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-120","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#8-keep-your-app-in-sync-with-webhooks","content":"Flip \"pending\" to \"subscribed\"; send a welcome email or a coupon"},"7769":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-121","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#8-keep-your-app-in-sync-with-webhooks","content":"`contact.unsubscribed`"},"7770":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-122","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#8-keep-your-app-in-sync-with-webhooks","content":"Turn off the matching setting in your app (`details.scope`: `all`, `list` or `topic`)"},"7771":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-123","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#8-keep-your-app-in-sync-with-webhooks","content":"`list.member_added` / `list.member_removed`"},"7772":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-124","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#8-keep-your-app-in-sync-with-webhooks","content":"Mirror list membership if you show it in your UI"},"7773":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-125","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#8-keep-your-app-in-sync-with-webhooks","content":"`email.opened` / `email.clicked`"},"7774":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-126","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#8-keep-your-app-in-sync-with-webhooks","content":"Engagement scoring, \"last seen\" in your CRM. Human activity only; bots are filtered."},"7775":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-127","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#8-keep-your-app-in-sync-with-webhooks","content":"`email.bounced`"},"7776":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-128","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#8-keep-your-app-in-sync-with-webhooks","content":"Ask the user to update their address"},"7777":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-129","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#8-keep-your-app-in-sync-with-webhooks","content":"A minimal handler:"},"7778":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-130","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#8-keep-your-app-in-sync-with-webhooks","content":"The Python SDK has a `WebhookPayload` model (`event_type`, `message_id`, `timestamp`, `recipient`, `details`); verify the signature with `hmac.compare_digest` over the raw body first, as shown in the Webhooks reference."},"7779":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-131","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#8-keep-your-app-in-sync-with-webhooks","content":"Respond within 10 seconds and do slow work asynchronously. Payload details are in the Webhooks reference."},"7780":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-132","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#9-import-an-existing-list","content":"Moving from another provider? Import the CSV straight into a list:"},"7781":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-133","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#9-import-an-existing-list","content":"The response reports `imported`, `skipped` (already existed), `addedToList` and per-row `errors`. Each request takes up to 1,000 rows and 2 MiB; split larger files."},"7782":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-134","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#9-import-an-existing-list","content":"With the SDKs:"},"7783":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-135","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#9-import-an-existing-list","content":"Before importing:"},"7784":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-136","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#9-import-an-existing-list","content":"Only import people who opted in to your mail. Imported contacts are recorded with consent source `import`."},"7785":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-137","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#9-import-an-existing-list","content":"Import your old provider's unsubscribes, bounces and complaints as suppressions first (`POST /api/v1/suppressions/bulk` with `reason` `Unsubscribe`, `Bounce` or `Complaint`), so they are never mailed."},"7786":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-138","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#9-import-an-existing-list","content":"Imports do not fire webhooks. Sync your app from your source data, not from webhooks, for the initial load."},"7787":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-139","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#10-bounce-and-complaint-protection","content":"NorthRelay protects your sender reputation, and the shared sending IP, automatically:"},"7788":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-140","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#10-bounce-and-complaint-protection","content":"A hard bounce adds a `Bounce` suppression; a spam complaint adds a `Complaint` suppression. Neither is ever lifted by a subscribe call, and both block even transactional mail."},"7789":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-141","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#10-bounce-and-complaint-protection","content":"Marketing sends also skip anyone who unsubscribed from everything or opted out of the topic the mail is sent under, and campaigns skip members who left the list or have not confirmed their double opt-in."},"7790":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-142","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#10-bounce-and-complaint-protection","content":"Adding an existing contact to a list does not make it mailable again: suppressed and unsubscribed members stay in the list but are skipped at send time and shown with `suppressionStatuses` in `GET /contacts/lists/{id}/members`."},"7791":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-143","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#10-bounce-and-complaint-protection","content":"Suppressed recipients are dropped before quota is counted."},"7792":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-144","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#10-bounce-and-complaint-protection","content":"Keep complaint rates low by using double opt-in, sending what people signed up for, putting the preference and unsubscribe links where they are easy to find, and removing people who have not engaged in a long time."},"7793":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-145","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#checklist","content":"Topics created, with public labels, and each list tagged with its topic"},"7794":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-146","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#checklist","content":"Signup calls `POST /subscriptions` from your server with `doubleOptIn`, `redirectUrl` and `consent`"},"7795":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-147","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#checklist","content":"Signup handler handles `RECIPIENT_UNSUBSCRIBED` and `RECIPIENT_SUPPRESSED`"},"7796":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-148","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#checklist","content